# Settings in the Phone topic: the landline that arrives over the internet.
# The operator sets all of it.
efecto-telefono_corte = The landline may lose service: if you turn it off, until you turn it back on; if you change a server, until the router reconnects to the operator.

## Phone line
ajuste-telefono-linea-titulo = Phone line
ajuste-telefono-linea-desc = The landline phone plugged into the router.
ajuste-telefono-linea-ayuda = The landline arrives over the internet and the operator sets it up. If it works properly, there is no need to touch anything here.
ajuste-telefono-linea-activa = Line on
ajuste-telefono-linea-activa-desc = If you turn it off, the landline can no longer make or receive calls.
ajuste-telefono-linea-silencio = Save during silences
ajuste-telefono-linea-silencio-desc = While nobody is speaking, the router stops sending sound to use less of the connection.
ajuste-telefono-linea-silencio-recomendado = Recommended if you have fibre or a good connection, as is usual today. Pros: the start of words is not cut off and the call does not seem to have dropped. Cons: each call uses a little more of the connection, which you will not notice with fibre.
ajuste-telefono-linea-contrasena = Line password
ajuste-telefono-linea-contrasena-desc = The password the line uses to sign in to the operator. The router won't let it be read, so to save any change on this card you have to type it; if you don't know it, ask the operator.
ajuste-telefono-linea-motivo = The line status can only be viewed: the router reports it.
ajuste-telefono-linea-en_servicio = Line status
ajuste-telefono-linea-en_servicio-desc = Whether the line is running on the router. It does not tell whether a phone is plugged in.
ajuste-telefono-linea-en_servicio-activa = Active
ajuste-telefono-linea-en_servicio-activa-desc = The line is running on the router, whether or not a phone is plugged in.
ajuste-telefono-linea-llamada = Call
ajuste-telefono-linea-llamada-desc = Whether a call is in progress right now.
ajuste-telefono-linea-llamada-sin_llamada = No call
ajuste-telefono-linea-llamada-sin_llamada-desc = There is no call in progress right now.

## Phone line: account and direct line
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-titulo = Line account and direct line
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-desc = The details the line uses to identify itself to the operator, and the automatic call when you pick up.
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-ayuda = The operator sets these. If you type one wrong, the landline stops working until you undo the change. To save any of them you have to type the line password, which the router won't let be read. Only change them if the operator asks you to.
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-usuario = Line user name
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-usuario-desc = The name the line uses to identify itself to the operator.
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-linea_directa = Direct line
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-linea_directa-desc = When you pick up, the phone calls a set number on its own: straight away or, if you do not dial anything, after a few seconds, depending on what the operator has set. If you do not know what it is for, leave it alone.
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-numero_directo = Direct line number
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-numero_directo-desc = The number that is called on its own while the direct line is on.
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-contrasena = Line password
ajuste-telefono-linea_oculto-contrasena-desc = The password the line uses to sign in to the operator. The router won't let it be read, so to save any change on this card you have to type it; if you don't know it, ask the operator.

## Calls
ajuste-telefono-sip-titulo = Keys and fax during calls
ajuste-telefono-sip-desc = How the keys you press during a call, and faxes, are sent.
ajuste-telefono-sip-ayuda = Keys matter in phone menus ("press 1 for…"). If a menu does not recognise what you press or a fax does not get through, this is what you can try.
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos = Keys during a call
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-desc = How the keys you press while a call is in progress reach the other end.
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-aparte = Separate from the voice
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-aparte-desc = Each key travels as its own signal, alongside the voice, so it does not depend on the sound quality.
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-en_la_voz = Inside the voice
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-en_la_voz-desc = The key beeps are mixed into the sound, as on an old phone. They can get lost if the call sounds poor.
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-mensajes = As call messages
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-mensajes-desc = Each key travels in a message separate from the sound. It only works if the operator supports it.
ajuste-telefono-sip-tonos-recomendado = Recommended if you use phone menus ("press 1 for…") or don't know. Pros: it is the most widespread way, and keys get through even if the call sounds poor. Cons: none significant for most people; if a menu does not recognise what you press, try another option.
ajuste-telefono-sip-fax = Fax over the internet
ajuste-telefono-sip-fax-desc = Sends faxes in a way designed for the internet, which copes better with small drop-outs. It only works if the operator supports it.

## Calls: operator's servers
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-titulo = Operator's phone servers
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-desc = The addresses the router connects to in order to make and receive calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-ayuda = The operator sets these. If you type one wrong, the landline stops working until you undo the change. Only change them if the operator asks you to.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-activo = Internet phone on
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-activo-desc = If you turn it off, the router stops connecting to the operator for calls and the landline does not work.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-activo-recomendado = Recommended if you have no landline phone plugged in. Pros: the router stops registering with the operator's voice server. Cons: the landline will not work, and the operator's remote management or a factory reset may turn it back on.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-motivo = The sign-up with the operator can only be viewed: the router reports it when it connects.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro = Sign-up with the operator
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro-desc = Whether the router is signed up with the operator's voice server, ready for landline calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro-registrada = Signed up
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro-registrada-desc = The router is signed up with the operator: the landline can make and receive calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro-sin_registrar = Not signed up
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-estado_registro-sin_registrar-desc = The router is not signed up with the operator: the landline cannot make or receive calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-dominio = Line domain
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-dominio-desc = The name of the operator's phone service, for example voz.example. No spaces or accented letters.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-servidor = Call server
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-servidor-desc = The address of the server that carries the calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-servidor_puerto = Call server port
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-servidor_puerto-desc = A number from 1 to 65535 given by the operator.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-registro = Sign-up server
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-registro-desc = The address of the server where the line signs up to receive calls.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-registro_puerto = Sign-up server port
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-registro_puerto-desc = A number from 1 to 65535 given by the operator.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-salida = Outgoing server
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-salida-desc = The address through which all calls go out to the operator.
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-salida_puerto = Outgoing server port
ajuste-telefono-sip_oculto-salida_puerto-desc = A number from 1 to 65535 given by the operator.

## Phone socket
ajuste-telefono-fisico-titulo = Fax, modem and alarms
ajuste-telefono-fisico-desc = For devices that are not phones and use the router's phone socket.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-ayuda = Some devices talk over the phone line with beeps: faxes, alarms, card terminals or old modems. If you have one and it cannot connect, check that its option is on.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-fax = Fax pass-through
ajuste-telefono-fisico-fax-desc = Treats faxes as untouched sound, so they arrive whole.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-modem = Modem pass-through
ajuste-telefono-fisico-modem-desc = Treats the beeps of alarms, card terminals and modems that call over the line as untouched sound.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-motivo = The socket status can only be viewed: the router reports it.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-puerto = Phone socket
ajuste-telefono-fisico-puerto-desc = Whether the router's phone socket is in service. It shows as in service even with no phone plugged in, so it does not tell whether there is one.
ajuste-telefono-fisico-puerto-true = In service
ajuste-telefono-fisico-puerto-false = Out of service
